The macOS app, the Windows installer and the Docker image include TorrServer
(https://github.com/YouROK/TorrServer), an unmodified separate program licensed
under the GNU General Public License v3. Moviestracker runs it as its own process
and talks to it over HTTP; its license and a link to its source travel with it.
TorrServer's Windows build carries a GStreamer runtime (LGPL) inside, which it
unpacks on first use; TorrServer's repository has its sources and build script.

The Docker image also contains Debian 13 and GStreamer with its plugins from
Debian, unmodified, each under its own license (see /usr/share/doc/*/copyright
in the image, and GSTREAMER.txt next to this file there for where to get their
sources).

The macOS app can download GStreamer (https://gstreamer.freedesktop.org), licensed
under the GNU Lesser General Public License, from its official site at the user's
request; it is not part of this source tree or of the release downloads.

